You have primary open-angle glaucoma in one or both eyes. This means the optic nerve is being damaged over time, usually because the pressure-related stress inside the eye is higher than that optic nerve can tolerate.\
\
Primary open-angle glaucoma usually develops slowly and painlessly. Side vision is often affected first, while central vision can stay normal until later stages. Because vision already lost from glaucoma cannot be restored, treatment is aimed at preventing further damage.\
